# Accepted trivy findings.
#
# Every entry here is a deliberate decision, not an unreviewed warning. Anything not
# listed is expected to pass. The reasoning is repeated in the relevant module README
# and in infra/README.md under "Simplifications".

# Load balancer is exposed publicly.
# It is the ingress tier and must be reachable, but its security group admits only
# CloudFront's origin-facing prefix list, not 0.0.0.0/0. The residual bypass risk is
# documented as a TODO in modules/s3_site/main.tf.
AWS-0053

# Listener does not use HTTPS.
# TLS terminates at CloudFront. This environment provisions no ACM certificate and no
# custom domain, so the ALB has no certificate to serve. Production adds an ACM
# certificate, an HTTPS listener and a redirect from 80.
AWS-0054

# Resources do not use a customer-managed KMS key.
# ECR repositories, CloudWatch log groups, the SNS topic, Performance Insights, the
# database secret and both S3 buckets all use AWS-managed keys. A CMK per service adds
# key administration and cost for data at this sensitivity; the decision would change
# for regulated or personal data.
AWS-0033
AWS-0017
AWS-0136
AWS-0078
AWS-0098
AWS-0132

# VPC does not have flow logs enabled.
# Not part of the architecture being represented, and it would need a log destination
# and delivery role to be useful. A production network module would enable it.
AWS-0178

# Instance does not have IAM authentication enabled.
# Credentials are held in Secrets Manager and injected by the ECS agent at task start.
# IAM database authentication is the stronger option and is a reasonable improvement,
# but it caps connections per second and would change how the application connects.
AWS-0176

# Instance does not have deletion protection enabled.
# Off in dev on purpose so the environment stays disposable. The variable defaults to
# true; terraform.tfvars overrides it for this environment only.
AWS-0177

# Access logging is disabled on the distribution and both buckets.
# Each needs a log destination bucket with a delivery policy and its own lifecycle
# rules. Out of scope for a single development environment.
AWS-0010
AWS-0089
